  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Capacity for More Effective Law Enforcement to Protect the Rarest of Chimpanzees: Nigeria-Cameroon Chimpanzees (Pan Troglodytes Ellioti and Pan Troglodytes Troglodytes) of Mbam&amp; Djerem National Park, Cameroon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to secure the long-term conservation of two chimpanzee subspecies in the Mbam &amp; Djerem National Park landscape through improved law enforcement and increased local capacity for protected area management. Specific activities include: (1) implementation of the SMART (Spatial Monitoring And Reporting Tool) law enforcement monitoring tool to better manage anti-poaching patrols; and (2) increase awareness and support for chimpanzee conservation in local communities through village and school education programs and collaboration with key stakeholders in the development of potential alternative and sustainable livelihood activities.</narrative>
  </description>
